 60   c  ABST$The 2003 evaluation of A=60 (2003Tu08) has been revised and       
 60  2c  brought up-to-date with references received by the cutoff date noted   
 60  3c  below.                                                                 
 60   c  COMM$Highlights and new data in this evaluation include: eight levels  
 60  2c  with energies up to 4861 keV (2006Zh42) in {+60}Cr, forty-four levels  
 60  3c  up to 9235 keV (2010St01) in {+60}Mn, and up to 17955 keV in {+60}Fe.  
 60  4c  These levels are from nuclear reactions with {+48}Ca projectiles on    
 60  5c  {+14}C targets, observed from |g-ray measurements using the            
 60  6c  GAMMASPHERE array of 101 germanium detectors.  Also, many new nuclear  
 60  7c  levels have been observed in {+60}Fe from {+14}C({+48}Ca,2n|g)         
 60  8c  (2007De56), and in {+60}Ni from {+59}Ni(n,|g) (2004Ra23),              
 60  9c  {+28}Si({+36}Ar,4p|g) (2008To15), and {+60}Ni(n,n'|g)                  
 60  Ac  (2002KoZT,2008Or02).                                                   
 60   c  The theoretical conversion coefficients for |g rays given in this      
 60  2c  evaluation are from 2002Ba85 and have been interpolated using the      
 60  3c  computer code BRICC (Band Raman Internal Conversion Coefficients)      
 60  4c  (2005KiZT).                                                            
 60   c  References 2011Me01, 2010Sh05 deal with production, and discovery of   
 60  2c  some nuclides.                                                         
 60   c  CUT$All data received by December 2012 have been evaluated.            
 60   c  ACKN$Thanks are due to Elizabeth (Libby) McCutchan for her thorough    
